<!--
  The Murmell mark: a murmur, drawn.

  Ink on a white plate, not a colour. The product's colour law says a saturated
  colour means "an agent" or "a person" — a house colour would be a third meaning,
  and would sit Murmell visually alongside the providers it is meant to sit
  underneath. The mark is the table, not a player at it.

  `28b400a` applied that law to the surfaces (App.tsx, Mark.tsx) but not here, so
  the tab kept the old orange-on-dark plate. The stroke is 2.6 to match Mark.tsx
  exactly: its comment claims the path is "verbatim from the favicon so the two can
  never drift apart", and the width has to hold that promise up too.

  The plate stays, unlike on a surface: a tiny fixed box in a tab strip needs a
  shape to be found by, where a bare line reads as a smudge.
-->
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" role="img" aria-label="Murmell">
  <rect width="32" height="32" rx="7" fill="#0f1218"/>
  <path d="M4 21 L8 21 L11 13 L14 24 L17 9 L20 19 L23 15 L28 15"
        fill="none" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="2.6"
        stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
</svg>
